    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26WA Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThis Part sets up a scheme for notification of eligible data\nbreaches.\n•\nAn eligible data breach happens if:\n\n(a)\nthere is unauthorised access to, unauthorised disclosure\nof, or loss of, personal information held by an entity;\nand\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\nNo. 12, 2017\n\n(b)\nthe access, disclosure or loss is likely to result in serious\nharm to any of the individuals to whom the information\nrelates.\n•\nAn entity must give a notification if:\n\n(a)\nit has reasonable grounds to believe that an eligible data\nbreach has happened; or\n\n(b)\nit is directed to do so by the Commissioner.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThis Part sets up a scheme for notification of eligible data\nbreaches.\n•\nAn eligible data breach happens if:\n\n(a)\nthere is unauthorised access to, unauthorised disclosure\nof, or loss of, personal information held by an entity;\nand\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\nNo. 12, 2017\n\n(b)\nthe access, disclosure or loss is likely to result in serious\nharm to any of the individuals to whom the information\nrelates.\n•\nAn entity must give a notification if:\n\n(a)\nit has reasonable grounds to believe that an eligible data\nbreach has happened; or\n\n(b)\nit is directed to do so by the Commissioner.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wa-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wa-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wa-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4b332ad9c78b5270d7297e37ba944195e1e474c3569e801539679b27ef973212",
      "skos:note": "An entity must give a notification if it has reasonable grounds to believe that an eligible data breach has happened or is directed to do so by the Commissioner."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26WA Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThis Part sets up a scheme for notification of eligible data\nbreaches.\n•\nAn eligible data breach happens if:\n\n(a)\nthere is unauthorised access to, unauthorised disclosure\nof, or loss of, personal information held by an entity;\nand\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\nNo. 12, 2017\n\n(b)\nthe access, disclosure or loss is likely to result in serious\nharm to any of the individuals to whom the information\nrelates.\n•\nAn entity must give a notification if:\n\n(a)\nit has reasonable grounds to believe that an eligible data\nbreach has happened; or\n\n(b)\nit is directed to do so by the Commissioner."
    },
