        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Likelihood that security measures can be overcome",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Harm likelihood is high if measures fail"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26WH Assessment of suspected eligible data breach",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an entity is aware that there are reasonable grounds to suspect\nthat there may have been an eligible data breach of the entity;\nand\n\n(b) the entity is not aware that there are reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the relevant circumstances amount to an eligible\ndata breach of the entity.\nAssessment\n\n(2) The entity must:\n\n(a) carry out a reasonable and expeditious assessment of whether\nthere are reasonable grounds to believe that the relevant\ncircumstances amount to an eligible data breach of the entity;\nand\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the assessment is\ncompleted within 30 days after the entity becomes aware as\nmentioned in paragraph (1)(a).\nNote:\nSection 26WK applies if an entity is aware that there are reasonable\ngrounds to believe that there has been an eligible data breach of the\nentity.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an entity is aware that there are reasonable grounds to suspect\nthat there may have been an eligible data breach of the entity;\nand\n\n(b) the entity is not aware that there are reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the relevant circumstances amount to an eligible\ndata breach of the entity.\nAssessment\n\n(2) The entity must:\n\n(a) carry out a reasonable and expeditious assessment of whether\nthere are reasonable grounds to believe that the relevant\ncircumstances amount to an eligible data breach of the entity;\nand\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the assessment is\ncompleted within 30 days after the entity becomes aware as\nmentioned in paragraph (1)(a).\nNote:\nSection 26WK applies if an entity is aware that there are reasonable\ngrounds to believe that there has been an eligible data breach of the\nentity.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wh-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26WH Assessment of suspected eligible data breach",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an entity is aware that there are reasonable grounds to suspect\nthat there may have been an eligible data breach of the entity;\nand\n\n(b) the entity is not aware that there are reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the relevant circumstances amount to an eligible\ndata breach of the entity.\nAssessment\n\n(2) The entity must:\n\n(a) carry out a reasonable and expeditious assessment of whether\nthere are reasonable grounds to believe that the relevant\ncircumstances amount to an eligible data breach of the entity;\nand\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the assessment is\ncompleted within 30 days after the entity becomes aware as\nmentioned in paragraph (1)(a).\nNote:\nSection 26WK applies if an entity is aware that there are reasonable\ngrounds to believe that there has been an eligible data breach of the\nentity."
    },
