    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wj-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exemption from notification obligations",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26WK Statement about eligible data breach",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an entity is aware that there are reasonable\ngrounds to believe that there has been an eligible data breach of the\nentity.\nStatement\n\n(2) The entity must:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) prepare a statement that complies with subsection (3);\nand\n\n(ii) give a copy of the statement to the Commissioner; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the entity becomes so\naware.\n\n(3) The statement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(i) must set out:\n\n(a) the identity and contact details of the entity; and\n\n(b) a description of the eligible data breach that the entity has\nreasonable grounds to believe has happened; and\n\n(c) the kind or kinds of information concerned; and\n\n(d) recommendations about the steps that individuals should take\nin response to the eligible data breach that the entity has\nreasonable grounds to believe has happened.\n\n(4) If the entity has reasonable grounds to believe that the access,\ndisclosure or loss that constituted the eligible data breach of the\nentity is an eligible data breach of one or more other entities, the\nstatement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(i) may also set out the\nidentity and contact details of those other entities.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an entity is aware that there are reasonable\ngrounds to believe that there has been an eligible data breach of the\nentity.\nStatement\n\n(2) The entity must:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) prepare a statement that complies with subsection (3);\nand\n\n(ii) give a copy of the statement to the Commissioner; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the entity becomes so\naware.\n\n(3) The statement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(i) must set out:\n\n(a) the identity and contact details of the entity; and\n\n(b) a description of the eligible data breach that the entity has\nreasonable grounds to believe has happened; and\n\n(c) the kind or kinds of information concerned; and\n\n(d) recommendations about the steps that individuals should take\nin response to the eligible data breach that the entity has\nreasonable grounds to believe has happened.\n\n(4) If the entity has reasonable grounds to believe that the access,\ndisclosure or loss that constituted the eligible data breach of the\nentity is an eligible data breach of one or more other entities, the\nstatement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(i) may also set out the\nidentity and contact details of those other entities.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wk-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wk-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wk-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26WK Statement about eligible data breach",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an entity is aware that there are reasonable\ngrounds to believe that there has been an eligible data breach of the\nentity.\nStatement\n\n(2) The entity must:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) prepare a statement that complies with subsection (3);\nand\n\n(ii) give a copy of the statement to the Commissioner; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the entity becomes so\naware.\n\n(3) The statement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(i) must set out:\n\n(a) the identity and contact details of the entity; and\n\n(b) a description of the eligible data breach that the entity has\nreasonable grounds to believe has happened; and\n\n(c) the kind or kinds of information concerned; and\n\n(d) recommendations about the steps that individuals should take\nin response to the eligible data breach that the entity has\nreasonable grounds to believe has happened.\n\n(4) If the entity has reasonable grounds to believe that the access,\ndisclosure or loss that constituted the eligible data breach of the\nentity is an eligible data breach of one or more other entities, the\nstatement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(i) may also set out the\nidentity and contact details of those other entities."
    },
