    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26WR(6) Commissioner may direct entity to notify eligible data breach",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(6) In deciding whether to give a direction to an entity under\nsubsection (1), the Commissioner must have regard to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) any relevant advice given to the Commissioner by:\n\n(i) an enforcement body; or\n\n(ii) the Australian Signals Directorate of the Defence\nDepartment;\n\n(b) any relevant submission that was made by the entity:\n\n(i) in response to an invitation under subsection (3); and\n\n(ii) within the period specified in the invitation;\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) In deciding whether to give a direction to an entity under\nsubsection (1), the Commissioner must have regard to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) any relevant advice given to the Commissioner by:\n\n(i) an enforcement body; or\n\n(ii) the Australian Signals Directorate of the Defence\nDepartment;\n\n(b) any relevant submission that was made by the entity:\n\n(i) in response to an invitation under subsection (3); and\n\n(ii) within the period specified in the invitation;\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a5763eacd7cd380d7a581e6ce682599ba29fc62b92865d739c5a66a59d4cfb33",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner must consider certain advice and submissions when deciding whether to direct an entity to notify a data breach."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26WR(6) Commissioner may direct entity to notify eligible data breach",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(6) In deciding whether to give a direction to an entity under\nsubsection (1), the Commissioner must have regard to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) any relevant advice given to the Commissioner by:\n\n(i) an enforcement body; or\n\n(ii) the Australian Signals Directorate of the Defence\nDepartment;\n\n(b) any relevant submission that was made by the entity:\n\n(i) in response to an invitation under subsection (3); and\n\n(ii) within the period specified in the invitation;\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the Commissioner considers\nrelevant."
    },
