    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26WR(8) Commissioner may direct entity to notify eligible data breach",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(8) If the Commissioner is aware that there are reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the access, disclosure or loss that constituted the\neligible data breach of the entity is an eligible data breach of one or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\nNo. 12, 2017\n\nmore other entities, a direction under subsection (1) may also\nrequire the statement referred to in paragraph (1)(a) to set out the\nidentity and contact details of those other entities.\nMethod of providing a statement to an individual",
      "skos:definition": "(8) If the Commissioner is aware that there are reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the access, disclosure or loss that constituted the\neligible data breach of the entity is an eligible data breach of one or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\nNo. 12, 2017\n\nmore other entities, a direction under subsection (1) may also\nrequire the statement referred to in paragraph (1)(a) to set out the\nidentity and contact details of those other entities.\nMethod of providing a statement to an individual",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffc69aeccf69e05e6410415ac624e92ff5266cb412c4311be7ac51caae8bff2b",
      "skos:note": "Entity must notify eligible data breach and provide additional information if required by the Commissioner.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wr-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26WR(8) Commissioner may direct entity to notify eligible data breach",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(8) If the Commissioner is aware that there are reasonable grounds to\nbelieve that the access, disclosure or loss that constituted the\neligible data breach of the entity is an eligible data breach of one or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\nNo. 12, 2017\n\nmore other entities, a direction under subsection (1) may also\nrequire the statement referred to in paragraph (1)(a) to set out the\nidentity and contact details of those other entities.\nMethod of providing a statement to an individual"
    },
    {
