      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity exempt from direction under subsection 26WR(1)",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Entity is an enforcement body",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Chief executive officer believes compliance would prejudice enforcement activities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26WT Exception—inconsistency with secrecy provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "Secrecy provisions\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, secrecy provision means a\nprovision that:\n\n(a) is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth (other than this\nAct); and\n\n(b) prohibits or regulates the use or disclosure of information.\n\n(2) If compliance by an entity with paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or\nsubsection 26WR(2) in relation to a statement would, to any extent,\nbe inconsistent with a secrecy provision (other than a prescribed\nsecrecy provision), paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or subsection 26WR(2),\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 12, 2017\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\n\nas the case may be, does not apply to the entity, in relation to the\nstatement, to the extent of the inconsistency.\nPrescribed secrecy provisions\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, prescribed secrecy provision\nmeans a secrecy provision that is specified in the regulations.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a prescribed secrecy provision:\n\n(a) paragraph 26WR(1)(b); and\n\n(b) subsection 26WR(2);\nare taken not to be provisions that require or authorise the use or\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(5) If compliance by an entity with paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or\nsubsection 26WR(2) in relation to a statement would, to any extent,\nbe inconsistent with a prescribed secrecy provision,\nparagraph 26WR(1)(b) or subsection 26WR(2), as the case may be,\ndoes not apply to the entity in relation to the statement.",
      "skos:definition": "Secrecy provisions\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, secrecy provision means a\nprovision that:\n\n(a) is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth (other than this\nAct); and\n\n(b) prohibits or regulates the use or disclosure of information.\n\n(2) If compliance by an entity with paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or\nsubsection 26WR(2) in relation to a statement would, to any extent,\nbe inconsistent with a secrecy provision (other than a prescribed\nsecrecy provision), paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or subsection 26WR(2),\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 12, 2017\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\n\nas the case may be, does not apply to the entity, in relation to the\nstatement, to the extent of the inconsistency.\nPrescribed secrecy provisions\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, prescribed secrecy provision\nmeans a secrecy provision that is specified in the regulations.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a prescribed secrecy provision:\n\n(a) paragraph 26WR(1)(b); and\n\n(b) subsection 26WR(2);\nare taken not to be provisions that require or authorise the use or\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(5) If compliance by an entity with paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or\nsubsection 26WR(2) in relation to a statement would, to any extent,\nbe inconsistent with a prescribed secrecy provision,\nparagraph 26WR(1)(b) or subsection 26WR(2), as the case may be,\ndoes not apply to the entity in relation to the statement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wt-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wt-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wt-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wt-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wt-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d8e7369e2afec497c8d6171ccbd03bbdaffb8c904dd848e6bac8a8ad976ebd67"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017#sch-1-sec-26wt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26WT Exception—inconsistency with secrecy provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "Secrecy provisions\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, secrecy provision means a\nprovision that:\n\n(a) is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth (other than this\nAct); and\n\n(b) prohibits or regulates the use or disclosure of information.\n\n(2) If compliance by an entity with paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or\nsubsection 26WR(2) in relation to a statement would, to any extent,\nbe inconsistent with a secrecy provision (other than a prescribed\nsecrecy provision), paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or subsection 26WR(2),\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 12, 2017\nPrivacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017\n\nas the case may be, does not apply to the entity, in relation to the\nstatement, to the extent of the inconsistency.\nPrescribed secrecy provisions\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, prescribed secrecy provision\nmeans a secrecy provision that is specified in the regulations.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a prescribed secrecy provision:\n\n(a) paragraph 26WR(1)(b); and\n\n(b) subsection 26WR(2);\nare taken not to be provisions that require or authorise the use or\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(5) If compliance by an entity with paragraph 26WR(1)(b) or\nsubsection 26WR(2) in relation to a statement would, to any extent,\nbe inconsistent with a prescribed secrecy provision,\nparagraph 26WR(1)(b) or subsection 26WR(2), as the case may be,\ndoes not apply to the entity in relation to the statement."
    },
